# SPR kernels: runtime and roofline

- CPU **Apple M4 Pro**, threads **6**, ISA `neon`; kernels: `spr.v5.b32`, `spr.v6.b32`
- speed-ups are vs **`spr.v5.b32`** (> 1 = faster); every number is the kernel's best k for that shape / sparsity

## 1. Machine ceilings (measured by `build/peaks`)

| ceiling | measured | datasheet |
|---|---|---|
| fp32 add, SIMD | 371.6 GFLOP/s | - |
| fp32 add, scalar | 93.3 GFLOP/s | - |
| read BW, L1 | 1008 GB/s | - |
| read BW, L2 | 636 GB/s | - |
| read BW, DRAM | 244 GB/s | - |

Ridge point (SIMD peak / DRAM BW): **1.52 flop/byte**: a kernel with lower intensity is DRAM-bound at best, higher intensity can reach the compute peak.

